      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1730256688834,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "Now lets try to understand HTTP method",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now lets try to understand HTTP method",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 228,
      "versionNonce": 107279053,
      "index": "bSm",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "gobBCTteNobbW3-SYOrOK",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 173.44911156934495,
      "y": 2498.784559289024,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 2262.006564458211,
      "height": 1125,
      "seed": 391001251,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1730256740867,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "HTTP Methods :as we got to know that http is nothing but a set of rule for client to communicate \nwith server or backend(Hyper Text Transfer Protocol) just like how us Human communicate\n\nlike we as Human when we want to communicate with each other or Transfer our thoughts with each other we use \nlanguage it can be english ,it can be hindi,it can be french ,it can be bengali etc so this language \nact as thought transfer protocol :\n\nSo using language we make ceratin sound and the  travel\nacross the air to the person we are trying to communicate\n\n\nPerson1->Hey------sounds travel through air->Person2\n\nPerson1<---Sound travel through air---Hi<--Person2\n\n\nSimilarly when computer want to talk to each other \nthey need HTTP or Hyper Text Transfer Protocol \n\nComp1--->req[http followed]--->Comp2[Server]\n[client]\n\n\nComp1<---[http followed]response---Comp2[Server]\n[client]",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HTTP Methods :as we got to know that http is nothing but a set of rule for client to communicate \nwith server or backend(Hyper Text Transfer Protocol) just like how us Human communicate\n\nlike we as Human when we want to communicate with each other or Transfer our thoughts with each other we use \nlanguage it can be english ,it can be hindi,it can be french ,it can be bengali etc so this language \nact as thought transfer protocol :\n\nSo using language we make ceratin sound and the  travel\nacross the air to the person we are trying to communicate\n\n\nPerson1->Hey------sounds travel through air->Person2\n\nPerson1<---Sound travel through air---Hi<--Person2\n\n\nSimilarly when computer want to talk to each other \nthey need HTTP or Hyper Text Transfer Protocol \n\nComp1--->req[http followed]--->Comp2[Server]\n[client]\n\n\nComp1<---[http followed]response---Comp2[Server]\n[client]",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 7,
      "versionNonce": 495019107,
      "index": "bSn",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "3zzykKVGF3nJ78mGNlfpu",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 201.02103279479422,
      "y": 3907.5823312588027,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1168.19921875,
      "height": 1305,
      "seed": 1390176749,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1730256786094,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "Lets learn the basic vocab for computer communication \nwhich are followed according to http \n\n\nRequest vocab:\n\n1.Get:Is the very first communication vocab in http\nand we use get when we need to Request or want server\nto response us with a resource needed by  the  user\nit cab be a html website,it can be a image ,a peice \nof data ...anything\n\n\n\n2.Post:In post req we send resource to server mostly\nby using a html form binded with a POST method to let \nthat html form know this will be used to post data and \nHence that where post req is used its basically used to\npost some data onto the server and receive a response\nrelated to data :\n\nExample :like we have a form in our website for signing \nup then our email and password will be posted to server\nin ordered to get registered on web site and out Server\nwill response with a peice of data like \"You are signed up\"\n\nor \"Thanks for signing\"-->this is done with a post Request\n\n",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lets learn the basic vocab for computer communication \nwhich are followed according to http \n\n\nRequest vocab:\n\n1.Get:Is the very first communication vocab in http\nand we use get when we need to Request or want server\nto response us with a resource needed by  the  user\nit cab be a html website,it can be a image ,a peice \nof data ...anything\n\n\n\n2.Post:In post req we send resource to server mostly\nby using a html form binded with a POST method to let \nthat html form know this will be used to post data and \nHence that where post req is used its basically used to\npost some data onto the server and receive a response\nrelated to data :\n\nExample :like we have a form in our website for signing \nup then our email and password will be posted to server\nin ordered to get registered on web site and out Server\nwill response with a peice of data like \"You are signed up\"\n\nor \"Thanks for signing\"-->this is done with a post Request\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1920412045,
      "index": "bSo",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "gmeKRnQtXIHEhcHsLE7DL",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 386.734566,
      "y": 5431.6575087472565,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1169.3992919921875,
      "height": 945,
      "seed": 457578509,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1730256804522,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "3.put :put request is for updating the resource via \ncompletely replacing the current resource with new resource\n\n4.patch:patch request is also used for updating but unlike \nput it does not completely replace the resource but \npatch it up with new resource ie old resource and new \nresource together :\n\n\nWe can understand this using a anology of amazon parcel:\nsuppose we ordered a bicycle from amazon and the rim of \ntyre is broken now when we got in touch with amazon\ncustomer service they offerd us two solution:\n\nsol1:replace the entire cycle with new one this is \nput request\n\n\nsol2:replace the old rim with new rim this is patch \nrequest\n",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3.put :put request is for updating the resource via \ncompletely replacing the current resource with new resource\n\n4.patch:patch request is also used for updating but unlike \nput it does not completely replace the resource but \npatch it up with new resource ie old resource and new \nresource together :\n\n\nWe can understand this using a anology of amazon parcel:\nsuppose we ordered a bicycle from amazon and the rim of \ntyre is broken now when we got in touch with amazon\ncustomer service they offerd us two solution:\n\nsol1:replace the entire cycle with new one this is \nput request\n\n\nsol2:replace the old rim with new rim this is patch \nrequest\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1756597955,
      "index": "bSp",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "8x8kNlYZcxpVPdw51uhkZ",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 425.5112150502906,
      "y": 6593.915801566909,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1108.79931640625,
      "height": 1665,
      "seed": 393865805,
      "groupIds": [],
