      "updated": 1730257663881,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "What are endpoints:\n\nsuppose we want to send letter to a friend that is\nif we have a pen pal in Europe or if we have a pen \npal in us or africa so the endpoint of the letter in http\nwill be http://hostName/endpoint\n\nhttp://hostName/europe or http://hostName/africa\n\n\nso this is about get method and not lets see other HTTP methods:\n\n\nBut to summerise http is a way for client to communicate with server \nside (database and backend handlers or api)and client side can be that a user \nuses to interact with our website so that could be our desktop,laptop or mobile\n\nbasically\n\nclient ->sends HTTP request->to->server\nclient<-receives an HTTP response from<-server\n",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What are endpoints:\n\nsuppose we want to send letter to a friend that is\nif we have a pen pal in Europe or if we have a pen \npal in us or africa so the endpoint of the letter in http\nwill be http://hostName/endpoint\n\nhttp://hostName/europe or http://hostName/africa\n\n\nso this is about get method and not lets see other HTTP methods:\n\n\nBut to summerise http is a way for client to communicate with server \nside (database and backend handlers or api)and client side can be that a user \nuses to interact with our website so that could be our desktop,laptop or mobile\n\nbasically\n\nclient ->sends HTTP request->to->server\nclient<-receives an HTTP response from<-server\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 60,
      "versionNonce": 1992468291,
      "index": "bSz",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "CWMOkZf_CCNstBA_JjOLh",
