      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1730257912587,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "and then once its done it send back a response info and \nresponse code\n\nnow for get method we dont need a frontend but for post request we need a form or api tool,\npatch,put and delete request can be handled with ajax js which are \nattached to form or via api tool but apart from get form post we need frontend like html form \nto get data from user but since creating frontend can take\ntime we will use api testing tool like rapidAPI and postman \n\nWe will use postman:\nIn POSTMAN we can target a specific url or endpoint and \nset our method-request so lets see how we can do that :\n",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "and then once its done it send back a response info and \nresponse code\n\nnow for get method we dont need a frontend but for post request we need a form or api tool,\npatch,put and delete request can be handled with ajax js which are \nattached to form or via api tool but apart from get form post we need frontend like html form \nto get data from user but since creating frontend can take\ntime we will use api testing tool like rapidAPI and postman \n\nWe will use postman:\nIn POSTMAN we can target a specific url or endpoint and \nset our method-request so lets see how we can do that :\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 487288995,
      "index": "bT5",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "EvUFkuScLq837YSGZ47tW",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 507.56473358459147,
      "y": 19628.120093956142,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 2097.9990234375,
      "height": 1305,
      "seed": 837424109,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1730257969979,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "/let see for post:\n\napp.post(\"/send\",(req,res)=>{\n    //to send data from client to server we should have\n    //a html frontend which can have form to take \n    //encoded data ,header or any message and that \n    //html form type should be POST so that we can send data to sevrer\n    //and then the function code written on that sever which works on that posted data will work on it\n    //and then the result will be sent back\n});\n\nlets take a example :\n\n<body>\n    <h1>Calculator</h1>\n    <form action=\"calculate\" method=\"POST\">\n        <label for=\"num1\">num1:</label>\n        <input type=\"text\" id=\"num1\" name=\"num1\">\n        <label for=\"num2\">num2:</label>\n        <input type=\"text\" id=\"num2\" name=\"num2\">\n        <label for=\"operation\">operation:</label>\n        <input type=\"text\" id=\"operation\" name=\"operation\">\n        <input type=\"submit\" value=\"Submit\">\n    </form>\n</body>\n\n\nso this a fairly simple frontend which contains a form to take two number and one character which will be\na operator and post that data",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "/let see for post:\n\napp.post(\"/send\",(req,res)=>{\n    //to send data from client to server we should have\n    //a html frontend which can have form to take \n    //encoded data ,header or any message and that \n    //html form type should be POST so that we can send data to sevrer\n    //and then the function code written on that sever which works on that posted data will work on it\n    //and then the result will be sent back\n});\n\nlets take a example :\n\n<body>\n    <h1>Calculator</h1>\n    <form action=\"calculate\" method=\"POST\">\n        <label for=\"num1\">num1:</label>\n        <input type=\"text\" id=\"num1\" name=\"num1\">\n        <label for=\"num2\">num2:</label>\n        <input type=\"text\" id=\"num2\" name=\"num2\">\n        <label for=\"operation\">operation:</label>\n        <input type=\"text\" id=\"operation\" name=\"operation\">\n        <input type=\"submit\" value=\"Submit\">\n    </form>\n</body>\n\n\nso this a fairly simple frontend which contains a form to take two number and one character which will be\na operator and post that data",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
