      "updated": 1730432852201,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Dynamic Routing/Route Parameter",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Dynamic Routing/Route Parameter",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KixE-wxgTgoNrUtfmMqwZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 811.6763784484557,
      "y": 45370.343209659026,
      "width": 624.7991333007812,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 755358029,
      "version": 173,
      "versionNonce": 823104205,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730434468629,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now what is dynamic routing and what is the use of dynamic\nrouting in making backend api\n\nDynamic Routes\nWhen you don't know the exact segment names ahead of time and want to \ncreate routes from dynamic data, you can use Dynamic Segments that are \nfilled in at request time or prerendered at build time.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now what is dynamic routing and what is the use of dynamic\nrouting in making backend api\n\nDynamic Routes\nWhen you don't know the exact segment names ahead of time and want to \ncreate routes from dynamic data, you can use Dynamic Segments that are \nfilled in at request time or prerendered at build time.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1IwZP-x5ZbKv7PIw5GvbM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 812.1141242712511,
      "y": 45544.978565062454,
      "width": 730.3989868164062,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1792592141,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 2078190765,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730434462893,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How Dynamic Routing Works in Express.js?\nDynamic routing in Express.js allows for creating flexible and customizable routes \nby incorporating parameters into the route paths. \nThese parameters are placeholders in the route, and their values can vary, enabling\nthe server to handle requests based on different input values.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How Dynamic Routing Works in Express.js?\nDynamic routing in Express.js allows for creating flexible and customizable routes \nby incorporating parameters into the route paths. \nThese parameters are placeholders in the route, and their values can vary, enabling\nthe server to handle requests based on different input values.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YqlfTgKi7HFcA1cvSWjRF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 817.366045694553,
      "y": 45686.78217315793,
      "width": 730.3989868164062,
      "height": 180,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1400439693,
      "version": 7,
      "versionNonce": 1286390883,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730434498412,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1.Define a Dynamic Route with Parameters: When defining a route in Express.js, \nyou can include parameters by specifying a colon followed by the parameter name in \nthe route path. For example:\n\n\napp.get('/users/:userId', (req, res) => {\nconst userId = req.params.userId;\nres.send(`User ID: ${userId}`);\n});",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1.Define a Dynamic Route with Parameters: When defining a route in Express.js, \nyou can include parameters by specifying a colon followed by the parameter name in \nthe route path. For example:\n\n\napp.get('/users/:userId', (req, res) => {\nconst userId = req.params.userId;\nres.send(`User ID: ${userId}`);\n});",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "GUAeP8JTgAiQwqBgKXq1u",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 799.4218327971006,
      "y": 45778.91086304443,
      "width": 389.0847461641785,
      "height": 91.90979360124766,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
