      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zWdEDZBgq4oHd8-CDeaNe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 818.6790494242476,
      "y": 45958.68197922827,
      "width": 665.5776312171025,
      "height": 164.3313023485078,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1768105155,
      "version": 94,
      "versionNonce": 437838061,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730434543084,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2.Accessing Parameters in the Route Handler: Inside the route handler function, \nyou can access the parameter values using req.params. In the example above, \nreq.params.userId would contain the value of the userId parameter from the URL.\n\n3.Requesting the Dynamic Route: To request the dynamic route, you would make a \nGET request to a URL that matches the defined route with the specified parameter. \nFor example, to access the user with ID 123:\nGET /users/123\n",
      "fontSize": 14.607226875422915,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2.Accessing Parameters in the Route Handler: Inside the route handler function, \nyou can access the parameter values using req.params. In the example above, \nreq.params.userId would contain the value of the userId parameter from the URL.\n\n3.Requesting the Dynamic Route: To request the dynamic route, you would make a \nGET request to a URL that matches the defined route with the specified parameter. \nFor example, to access the user with ID 123:\nGET /users/123\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "zIznsgsgIBdK7ZS1Jac2t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 819.5541904618005,
      "y": 46138.124902914344,
      "width": 725.4736907142487,
      "height": 109.92040864631002,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1740059555,
      "version": 106,
      "versionNonce": 712452515,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730434576773,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4.Handling the Request: When a request is made to the dynamic route, \nExpress.js matches the URL to the defined route pattern and extracts the parameter value. \nIn this case, it would extract the userId from the URL.\n\n5.Using the Parameter Value: The parameter value extracted from the URL can then be used \nwithin the route handler to customize the server’s response based on the parameter value.",
      "fontSize": 14.656054486174671,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4.Handling the Request: When a request is made to the dynamic route, \nExpress.js matches the URL to the defined route pattern and extracts the parameter value. \nIn this case, it would extract the userId from the URL.\n\n5.Using the Parameter Value: The parameter value extracted from the URL can then be used \nwithin the route handler to customize the server’s response based on the parameter value.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2nb90p8QcumFJA5uQa2Y4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 822.6180372394624,
      "y": 46288.463105374445,
      "width": 695.6656432461659,
      "height": 106.58834651413126,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
