      "updated": 1730446339202,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now why did this happend,the reason is that our code executes top to \nbottom \n\nso when we hit a new route server get reloaded or called again in order \nto fetch the code which is binded to that route in starts reading it from\nthe top now the problem is both our dynamic route and static route are decalred after \n\"/\" which is home the root route and since :user is dynamic in nature so when \nwe type in url bar localhost/user this \"/user\" instead of getting interpreted\nas the static \"/user route\" it got interpretes that \"user\" is  value form dynamic \nroute \":user_name\" so it executed that code \n\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now why did this happend,the reason is that our code executes top to \nbottom \n\nso when we hit a new route server get reloaded or called again in order \nto fetch the code which is binded to that route in starts reading it from\nthe top now the problem is both our dynamic route and static route are decalred after \n\"/\" which is home the root route and since :user is dynamic in nature so when \nwe type in url bar localhost/user this \"/user\" instead of getting interpreted\nas the static \"/user route\" it got interpretes that \"user\" is  value form dynamic \nroute \":user_name\" so it executed that code \n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
