      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730450858883,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Understanding Post Request \n---------------------------",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Understanding Post Request \n---------------------------",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2TT6C4elXlYAKInU8JRNJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 567.7649422788086,
      "y": 56035.969127174845,
      "width": 686.3990478515625,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 814617938,
      "version": 134,
      "versionNonce": 1299809682,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730450934125,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A POST request is an HTTP method used to send data to a server to create or \nupdate a resource. It is commonly used when submitting forms or \nuploading files to server or mostly to database like sql or no-sql db\nlike mongodb. Unlike GET requests, which append data to the URL as \nquery parameters, POST requests send data in the request body or also know\nas body payload, making it more secure and capable of handling larger amounts \nof data.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A POST request is an HTTP method used to send data to a server to create or \nupdate a resource. It is commonly used when submitting forms or \nuploading files to server or mostly to database like sql or no-sql db\nlike mongodb. Unlike GET requests, which append data to the URL as \nquery parameters, POST requests send data in the request body or also know\nas body payload, making it more secure and capable of handling larger amounts \nof data.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "R2CYCmdPKKSCpp_Wx5pDL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 567.5969216941533,
      "y": 56199.347083292014,
      "width": 739.198974609375,
      "height": 220,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 733923602,
      "version": 65,
      "versionNonce": 1206431822,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730451021928,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key Features of POST Requests\n1.Data in the Body:POST requests send data in the request body, \nallowing for more complex and larger payloads than what can be sent in a URL.\n\n2.Non-Idempotent:Each POST request can result in a different outcome. For example, \nsubmitting the same form multiple times might create multiple entries on the server.\n\n3.Common Use Cases:\n->Submitting forms (e.g., user registration, login).\n->Uploading files (e.g., images, documents).\n->Creating new resources (e.g., creating a new blog post).",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key Features of POST Requests\n1.Data in the Body:POST requests send data in the request body, \nallowing for more complex and larger payloads than what can be sent in a URL.\n\n2.Non-Idempotent:Each POST request can result in a different outcome. For example, \nsubmitting the same form multiple times might create multiple entries on the server.\n\n3.Common Use Cases:\n->Submitting forms (e.g., user registration, login).\n->Uploading files (e.g., images, documents).\n->Creating new resources (e.g., creating a new blog post).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2GtlLl74klwwEwC-9FYut",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 568.5328520012185,
      "y": 56509.93939735045,
      "width": 8.79998779296875,
      "height": 20,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1136756498,
      "version": 9,
      "versionNonce": 733044626,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730451095369,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uszRBHUPT2Ab_WXRO8ba6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 549.5269008266282,
      "y": 56464.46239813872,
      "width": 598.5991821289062,
      "height": 240,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 723965074,
      "version": 124,
      "versionNonce": 745163666,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730451159996,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Sending POST Requests from a Browser\nWhile you can send GET requests directly from a browser's address\nbar by typing in a URL, sending a POST request directly from the\nbrowser is not straightforward. Here’s why:\n\n1.No Direct URL Access:Browsers do not allow you to enter POST data\ndirectly in the address bar. The address bar is designed for GET\nrequests, where data can be appended as query parameters.\n\n2.Need for a Form:\nTo send a POST request, you typically use an HTML form with a method\nattribute set to POST. Here’s a simple example:",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Sending POST Requests from a Browser\nWhile you can send GET requests directly from a browser's address bar by typing in a URL, sending a POST request directly from the browser is not straightforward. Here’s why:\n\n1.No Direct URL Access:Browsers do not allow you to enter POST data directly in the address bar. The address bar is designed for GET requests, where data can be appended as query parameters.\n\n2.Need for a Form:\nTo send a POST request, you typically use an HTML form with a method attribute set to POST. Here’s a simple example:",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "AYdXpNKw91uIvl6A6QLZa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 549.9873336183725,
      "y": 56747.6070525897,
      "width": 605.399169921875,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVT",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1858340302,
      "version": 56,
      "versionNonce": 1921885582,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730451155820,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "<form action=\"/submit\" method=\"POST\">\n    <input type=\"text\" name=\"username\" placeholder=\"Username\"\nrequired>\n    <input type=\"password\" name=\"password\" placeholder=\"Password\"\nrequired>\n    <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n</form>",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "<form action=\"/submit\" method=\"POST\">\n    <input type=\"text\" name=\"username\" placeholder=\"Username\" required>\n    <input type=\"password\" name=\"password\" placeholder=\"Password\" required>\n    <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n</form>",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "zIUtWKuLp_W99ZSnNa04G",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 543.5697648694642,
      "y": 56944.42194644891,
      "width": 580.7991943359375,
      "height": 40,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVU",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1002677006,
      "version": 62,
      "versionNonce": 886094738,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730451171457,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When the user fills out this form and clicks \"Submit,\" the browser\nwill send a POST request to the specified action URL (/submit).",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When the user fills out this form and clicks \"Submit,\" the browser will send a POST request to the specified action URL (/submit).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "md9R31aGFongATUdXrWWe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 542.5338659445772,
      "y": 57232.00672015148,
      "width": 580.9992065429688,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1851273998,
      "version": 231,
      "versionNonce": 620666382,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730451261644,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3.JavaScript/AJAX:\n\nYou can also use JavaScript (with fetch or XMLHttpRequest) to send\nPOST requests programmatically. This allows for more dynamic\ninteractions without requiring a page reload.\nExample using fetch:\n\njavascript-code\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nfetch('/submit', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: {\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ username: 'testuser', password:\n'testpass' }),\n})\n.then(response => response.json())\n.then(data => console.log(data))\n.catch(error => console.error('Error:', error));",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3.JavaScript/AJAX:\n\nYou can also use JavaScript (with fetch or XMLHttpRequest) to send POST requests programmatically. This allows for more dynamic interactions without requiring a page reload.\nExample using fetch:\n\njavascript-code\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nfetch('/submit', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: {\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ username: 'testuser', password: 'testpass' }),\n})\n.then(response => response.json())\n.then(data => console.log(data))\n.catch(error => console.error('Error:', error));",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
