      "crop": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iyejAFYmqSQ5bxgXxF7YH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 565.4457660073848,
      "y": 61744.03847275974,
      "width": 580.7991943359375,
      "height": 40,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bW5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1502528018,
      "version": 57,
      "versionNonce": 1045685266,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730455242172,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In this example, when the form is submitted, the data will be sent\nto /submit.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In this example, when the form is submitted, the data will be sent to /submit.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Ch3hKvm_h_4Ir6MrjkJr0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 558.606158906269,
      "y": 61860.3979917224,
      "width": 589.7991943359375,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bWD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 685526414,
      "version": 77,
      "versionNonce": 1233481042,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730455318826,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. method Attribute\n->Definition: The method attribute defines the HTTP method to be\nused when sending form data. The two most common methods are GET\nand POST.\n\na)GET:\nSends form data as part of the URL query string.\nUseful for retrieving data, and the data is visible in the URL.\nLimited in the amount of data that can be sent.\n\nExample:\nform action=\"/search\" method=\"GET\">\n    <input type=\"text\" name=\"query\">\n    <button type=\"submit\">Search</button>\n</form>\n\nHere, if you enter a search query and submit the form, the URL will\nlook like /search?query=your_search_term.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. method Attribute\n->Definition: The method attribute defines the HTTP method to be used when sending form data. The two most common methods are GET and POST.\n\na)GET:\nSends form data as part of the URL query string.\nUseful for retrieving data, and the data is visible in the URL.\nLimited in the amount of data that can be sent.\n\nExample:\nform action=\"/search\" method=\"GET\">\n    <input type=\"text\" name=\"query\">\n    <button type=\"submit\">Search</button>\n</form>\n\nHere, if you enter a search query and submit the form, the URL will look like /search?query=your_search_term.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZGoXxtJOdklbhsP207cLi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 530.162108700446,
      "y": 62280.38318287016,
      "width": 589.5991821289062,
      "height": 340,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bWE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 125294226,
      "version": 68,
      "versionNonce": 1089907406,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730455364298,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "b)POST:\nSends form data as part of the request body.\nMore secure for sending sensitive information, as the data is not\nvisible in the URL.\nCan handle larger amounts of data.\n\nExample:\n\nhtml\n<form action=\"/submit\" method=\"POST\">\n    <input type=\"text\" name=\"username\">\n    <input type=\"password\" name=\"password\">\n    <button type=\"submit\">Login</button>\n</form>\n\nIn this case, the username and password will be sent in the body of\nthe request, keeping them hidden from the URL.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "b)POST:\nSends form data as part of the request body.\nMore secure for sending sensitive information, as the data is not visible in the URL.\nCan handle larger amounts of data.\n\nExample:\n\nhtml\n<form action=\"/submit\" method=\"POST\">\n    <input type=\"text\" name=\"username\">\n    <input type=\"password\" name=\"password\">\n    <button type=\"submit\">Login</button>\n</form>\n\nIn this case, the username and password will be sent in the body of the request, keeping them hidden from the URL.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
