      "updated": 1730563229696,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here we have to understand how spread operator \nso suppose we have two object \nlet a={name:\"max\",age:18};\nlet b={age:19}\n\nlet c={...a,...b}\n...a will iterate through o object and takeout \nor fetch out each key pair:\n\nname:\"max\"\nage:18\n\nsimilarly:(...b)=age:19\nc={name:\"max\",age:18,age:19}--nowe key should be \nunique so last value will override the previous value\n\n",
      "fontSize": 11.763080659380908,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here we have to understand how spread operator \nso suppose we have two object \nlet a={name:\"max\",age:18};\nlet b={age:19}\n\nlet c={...a,...b}\n...a will iterate through o object and takeout \nor fetch out each key pair:\n\nname:\"max\"\nage:18\n\nsimilarly:(...b)=age:19\nc={name:\"max\",age:18,age:19}--nowe key should be \nunique so last value will override the previous value\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
